2. Objective

Enable secure user login using OAuth 2.0 via Azure AD B2C, validate JWT tokens in the backend, and store the user’s tokens for future API access.


---

3. Assumptions & Dependencies

Azure AD B2C is configured with user flows

ASP.NET Core 7 Web API

Dapper for DB interaction

SQL Server as data store

Users are pre-registered in B2C or social logins are enabled



---

4. Design Overview

🔁 Login Flow

1. Frontend redirects user to Azure B2C login


2. User logs in and receives ID token + Access token


3. Frontend sends ID token to Web API


4. API validates the JWT using B2C public keys


5. If valid, user record is stored/retrieved in the DB


6. Tokens (or identifiers) are saved for reference/logging




---

5. Class Design

public class AuthController : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpPost("api/auth/login")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> Login([FromBody] TokenRequest request);
}

public class TokenValidatorService
{
    public ClaimsPrincipal ValidateToken(string idToken);
}

public class UserService
{
    public Task<User> GetOrCreateUserAsync(ClaimsPrincipal userClaims);
}

public class UserRepository
{
    public Task<User> GetUserByEmailAsync(string email);
    public Task CreateUserAsync(User user);
}


---

6. Method Details

Login(TokenRequest request)

Input: { string IdToken }

Output: 200 OK with user details / 401 Unauthorized

Steps:

Validate JWT

Parse claims (email, name, sub)

Check if user exists in DB

If not, create new user

Return user info



ValidateToken(string idToken)

Uses Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens to validate against Azure B2C public keys

Returns ClaimsPrincipal or throws SecurityTokenException



