7. Database Design

Table: Users | Column       | Type        | Notes                      | |--------------|-------------|----------------------------| | Id           | GUID        | Primary Key                | | Email        | NVARCHAR(100)| Unique, required           | | DisplayName  | NVARCHAR(100)|                            | | B2CId        | NVARCHAR(200)| Maps to B2C sub claim    | | CreatedAt    | DATETIME    | Default = GETDATE()        |


---

8. API Contract

POST /api/auth/login

Request:

{
  "idToken": "<JWT received from B2C>"
}

Response:

{
  "userId": "guid",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "displayName": "John Doe"
}

Errors:

401 Unauthorized: Invalid token

500 Internal Server Error: DB issues



---

9. Security Considerations

Token is validated using Azure AD B2C's JWKS endpoint

No token is stored permanently in DB (only subject ID & email)

HTTPS only

Input is sanitized



---

10. Configuration

appsettings.json:

{
  "AzureAdB2C": {
    "Instance": "https://<tenant>.b2clogin.com",
    "ClientId": "<client-id>",
    "Tenant": "<tenant-name>",
    "SignUpSignInPolicyId": "B2C_1_signin"
  }
}

Startup Registration:

services.AddAuthentication(JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)
    .AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApi(Configuration.GetSection("AzureAdB2C"));


